<div class="path-head"><p class="featured-region">Reading path · 8 stops</p><h1 class="path-title">Wonders and Monuments</h1><p class="path-tagline">What the great builders left standing.</p><p class="path-intro">Stone keeps promises that documents cannot. This path visits eight monuments, from the one surviving ancient wonder to a Mughal tomb, reading each as evidence: of the state that raised it, the labour that built it, and the beliefs it was meant to outlast.</p><p class="path-types">Suits <a href="/start">the Builder</a> · <a href="/start">the Navigator</a></p></div>
<ol class="path-steps"><li><a class="path-step" href="/encyclopedia/great-pyramid-of-giza"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/great-pyramid-of-giza.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">1 · Encyclopedia · Work · c. 2560 BCE</span><span class="path-step-name">Great Pyramid of Giza</span><span class="path-step-why">The oldest of the seven wonders and the only one still standing.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/encyclopedia/great-wall-of-china"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/great-wall-of-china.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">2 · Encyclopedia · Work</span><span class="path-step-name">Great Wall of China</span><span class="path-step-why">Two thousand years of walls against the steppe, joined into one idea.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/encyclopedia/petra"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/petra.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">3 · Encyclopedia · Place</span><span class="path-step-name">Petra</span><span class="path-step-why">A caravan city carved into rose-red rock at the crossroads of incense routes.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/encyclopedia/hagia-sophia"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hagia-sophia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">4 · Encyclopedia · Work · 537 CE</span><span class="path-step-name">Hagia Sophia</span><span class="path-step-why">Justinian's dome, church then mosque then museum then mosque, fifteen centuries at the centre of two faiths.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/encyclopedia/angkor-wat"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/angkor-wat.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">5 · Encyclopedia · Work</span><span class="path-step-name">Angkor Wat</span><span class="path-step-why">The largest religious monument on earth, the Khmer state in stone.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/encyclopedia/alhambra"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alhambra.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">6 · Encyclopedia · Work</span><span class="path-step-name">Alhambra</span><span class="path-step-why">The last palace of al-Andalus, beauty built on a falling frontier.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/encyclopedia/machu-picchu"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/machu-picchu.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">7 · Encyclopedia · Place</span><span class="path-step-name">Machu Picchu</span><span class="path-step-why">An Inca royal estate the conquest never found.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/encyclopedia/taj-mahal"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/taj-mahal.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">8 · Encyclopedia · Work</span><span class="path-step-name">Taj Mahal</span><span class="path-step-why">The Mughal empire's wealth and craft condensed into one tomb.</span></span></a></li></ol>
